      236.95,
      227.66,
      394.53,
      238.33
    ],
    "text": "SCHEDULE(Section 5B)",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      246.62,
      397.14,
      266.29
    ],
    "text": "1. A person shall be disqualified from being appointed or continuingas a member of the Committee\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      273.62,
      397.01,
      293.29
    ],
    "text": "(a)if he is or becomes a Member of Parliament, a ProvincialCouncil or any local authority;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      300.62,
      365.61,
      311.29
    ],
    "text": "(b)if he is not or ceases to be a citizen of Sri Lanka;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      174.43,
      318.62,
      397.02,
      338.29
    ],
    "text": "(c)if he is under any law in force in Sri Lanka or in any othercountry, found or declared to be of unsound mind;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      173.71,
      345.62,
      397.35,
      365.29
    ],
    "text": "(d)if he is serving or has served a sentence of imprisonmentimposed by any court in Sri Lanka or any other country; or",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      174.43,
      372.62,
      397.15,
      392.29
    ],
    "text": "(e)if he had been removed from membership of the Committeefor misconduct.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      399.62,
      397.07,
      437.29
    ],
    "text": "2. Every appointed member shall, unless he vacates office earlierby death, resignation or removal, hold office for a term of three yearsfrom the date of his appointment and unless he has been removedfrom office, be eligible for re-appointment.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      444.98,
      397.38,
      484.45
    ],
    "text": "3. The Minister may by Order published in the Gazette, removefrom office the appointed member of the Committee for physical ormental incapacity or for any act or thing which in the opinion of theMinister is likely to bring disrepute to the Committee.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      483.74,
      397.39,
      544.93
    ],
    "text": "4. Where an appointed member of the Committee is, by reason ofillness, infirmity or absence from Sri Lanka for a period not less thanthree months, is temporarily unable to perform his duties, it shall bethe duty of such member to inform the Minister in writing of suchinability. The Minister may having regard to section 5B, appoint someother person to act in his place during the absence.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      5.599999904632568,
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      554.42,
      397.21,
      585.37
    ],
    "text": "5. The members of the Committee shall be remunerated in suchmanner and at such rates as may be determined by the Minister, inconsultation with the Minister in charge of the subject of Finance.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      594.38,
      397.26,
      633.49
    ],
    "text": "6. (1) The Chairman of the Committee shall if present, preside atall meetings of the Committee. In the absence of the Chairman fromany such meeting, the Commissioner General of Labour shall presideat such meeting.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 7,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      642.02,
      397.41,
      662.29
    ],
    "text": "(2) An ex-officio member may at any time by prior notice inwriting, nominate his deputy to represent him at any meeting of the",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
